By the reflection-generation theorem, an element of $O(2)$ is a product of at most two reflections. The determinant of a reflection is $-1$. If the determinant is $-1$, the element is one reflection. If the determinant is $1$, it is either the identity or a product of two reflections in nonparallel planes.

A product of two reflections in nonparallel planes fixes only the origin: a nonzero fixed vector would make the two normal vectors parallel. Hence a nonidentity element of $SO(2)$ is a rotation about $O$.
